      },
      {
        "id": "jep-416-constant",
        "says": "Since JDK 18 Method.invoke is built on method handles, and the JIT inlines through it only when the Method is a constant such as a static final field.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Concept Explanation"
        ],
        "exercise": "quiz",
        "reason": null
      },
      {
        "id": "lambda-metafactory",
        "says": "LambdaMetafactory turns a MethodHandle into a functional interface implementation that the JIT inlines like a lambda.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Interview Q&A Section",
          "example:41-reflection/README_10.3.4.md:17",
          "example:41-reflection/README_10.3.4.md:16"
        ],
        "exercise": null,
        "reason": "its result behaves exactly like a direct call and its only gain is speed, which no deterministic test can observe"
      },
      {
        "id": "method-handle",
        "says": "A MethodHandle is a typed reference whose access is checked at lookup, and invokeExact calls it with its exact type, without boxing or an Object array.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Interview Q&A Section",
          "example:41-reflection/README_10.3.4.md:9",
